{"id": "EUVD-2026-81848", "enisaUuid": "9b7d075b-a980-3c19-8a90-770c78b5b15c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_conn: fix the SCO setup context lifetime\n\nhci_setup_sync() queues a conn_handle_t with a NULL destroy callback, so\nthe context is only freed if hci_enhanced_setup_sync() actually runs. An\nentry that is cancelled instead is leaked, as\n_hci_cmd_sync_cancel_entry() does not release entry->data when there is\nno destroy callback, and hci_cmd_sync_clear() cancels every pending entry\nwhen the controller is unregistered.\n\nThe context also stores a bare hci_conn pointer, so the connection can be\nfreed while the work is queued. The dequeue in hci_conn_del() does not\ncover it either, as it matches on entry->data == conn and entry->data is\nthe wrapper here. Same problem as commit 2f5d635ad590 (\"Bluetooth:\nhci_sync: hold conn in hci_connect_acl/le_sync() callbacks\").\n\nHold the connection and release both from a destroy callback. The\nsubmission failure path drops both, since hci_cmd_sync_submit() does not\ncall the destroy callback when it fails to queue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:31", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37cfec41365c826d5496ef5d00c9e215eee53aa2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a2ba69cebe3fc5a3d4fa8eaaad3c42862723c27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a661de0ee29d0915c5e924edf91d2be2b4d35bae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1fe3c74a89a7749cba3caa0dd91236049c66116", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d7b1c834d2775b73c65e4888e01f5af8b477fe9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42de40abe25db9211107af8896d0fd741f10648d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90255", "GHSA-wjxp-4hww-crmx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07a145e7-728f-3597-bd5b-4c5a59d0f537", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e07a06b4eb417f5271d33ce2240e93c62d98b7b4 <37cfec41365c826d5496ef5d00c9e215eee53aa2"}, {"id": "130e54dc-59fa-3c9e-94c4-739695fb42d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e07a06b4eb417f5271d33ce2240e93c62d98b7b4 <42de40abe25db9211107af8896d0fd741f10648d"}, {"id": "66b83aae-3924-317e-9c9f-d1ff5d16ad71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "80af0001-7547-369d-80bd-50727390ecaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8533f974-1f51-3a71-b03f-5fd7bec82325", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e07a06b4eb417f5271d33ce2240e93c62d98b7b4 <4d7b1c834d2775b73c65e4888e01f5af8b477fe9"}, {"id": "a5188844-00a3-3aad-8166-ea10227c6341", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e07a06b4eb417f5271d33ce2240e93c62d98b7b4 <c1fe3c74a89a7749cba3caa0dd91236049c66116"}, {"id": "a565200a-e8a8-3432-9c03-77185e72ddab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "a812cb4b-60c7-3c37-a9e7-f2267f3e4a20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e07a06b4eb417f5271d33ce2240e93c62d98b7b4 <9a2ba69cebe3fc5a3d4fa8eaaad3c42862723c27"}, {"id": "adc7d76c-71b4-338c-9014-d92588f92388", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b6481d65-afd4-39c3-a58b-b66c3cfb19d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "b6bce3bc-8ffe-342f-b0e7-3060bb447004", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e07a06b4eb417f5271d33ce2240e93c62d98b7b4 <a661de0ee29d0915c5e924edf91d2be2b4d35bae"}, {"id": "d3345e51-f8a4-39d5-a812-9796a03a23de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linu